(
 '* 0.54.1 ⋄ 2026-09-29'
 '  * Bug fix: CreateProject did not behave well when no argument was provided'
 '  * Internal changes '
 '* 0.54.0 ⋄ 2026-09-19'
 '  * New version of APLGit2 should show the line-drawing chars (]Status) correctly.'
 '  * New version of CommTools gives much more powerful options to the user for selecting from a list'
 '  * On opening a project, a package whose installed version is not hosted by any Registry any'
 '    more is now reported: such a project cannot be set up from scratch. So are packages that'
 '    did not come from tatin.dev, which used to be mentioned only when no later version was'
 '    found for anything at all.'
 '  * A package the very same version of which is hosted by a Registry other than the one it was'
 '    installed from is now named, together with both URLs. That is what a package looks like'
 '    that was installed from a local Registry before being published. Cider then offers to'
 '    re-install that folder from its dependency list, which rebuilds it from scratch without'
 '    moving any version: the automation ID is "ReInstallFromDependencies@", and'
 '    checkPackageVersions=2 answers it automatically.'
 '  * Only a genuinely later version is offered for updating now. A package that merely turned'
 '    up on a different Registry, or one that is not available any more, was offered as well,'
 '    and the re-install that followed could replace it by an earlier version.'
 '  * The automation ID of the "Report Git status?" question was misspelled and is now'
 '    "HowToReportGitStatus@". Anybody automating that question must adjust the ID.'
 '  * "CloseProject" accepts one *or* two integers as left argument now: [1] is "performChecks" as'
 '    before and [2] is "batch", which tells Cider that nobody is there to answer a question. A'
 '    single integer keeps its former meaning, so existing calls are unaffected.'
 '  * Check for Dropbox conflicts removed: a Git managed folder should *never* be watched by'
 '    something like Dropbox!'
 '  * Gits status report improved in terms of readability'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * A project that failed to open could be neither closed nor opened again. The configuration is'
 '      now injected as soon as the Link exists rather than at the very end, so a project that throws'
 '      on the way is still recognised as open, is listed by "]Cider.ListOpenProjects" and can be '
 '      closed with "]Cider.CloseProject". Before that only ⎕SE.Link.Break by hand or )CLEAR got you '
 '      out, and in batch mode Cider went there by design.'
 '    * When the "lx" function of a project crashed, the report named neither the error nor the'
 '      return code: the message was overwritten by the headline, which was then spelled out one'
 '      character per line as the supposed detail.'
 '    * Two messages were assembled with a comma missing, so they came out nested and `Assert`'
 '      signalled a DOMAIN ERROR in place of the text: a crashing "ExecuteAfterProjectOpen", and'
 '      "]Cider.AddNuGetDependencies" reporting an invalid package name.'
 '    * The Git status report was mangled when the repository had no commits yet, and whenever there '
 '      was at least one stash: those lines were spread out one character per column and padded the '
 '      whole report to their length. '
 '    * The list of later versions cut a fixed number of characters off the "Latest" column in order '
 '      to show just the version number. Anything that was not a package ID, like one of Tatin''s '
 '      "<<< ... >>>" markers, came out as a fragment'
 '    * NuGet packages were refused outright whenever Dyalog was running under .NET Framework rather'
 '      than .NET, although the simpler ones work there perfectly well. "OpenProject" and'
 '      "LoadNuGetDependencies" asked two different questions, so Cider first decided the packages'
 '      could be loaded and then declined to load them. Both ask "HasDotNet" now, and a package that'
 '      really does need .NET says so itself.'
 '    * With "HandleLinkStops" set to 1 ("ask me") Cider asked whether stops saved in ".linkconfig"'
 '      should be deleted even when there was nobody to answer, so an unattended run could sit there'
 '      waiting. Nothing is done in that case now; 2 still deletes them without asking.'
 '    * The third column of "]Cider.ListOpenProjects -verbose" holds the number of objects again, as'
 '      the documentation has always said. Link 4 (Dyalog 19.0) added a column to the result of'
 '      "Link.Status" and renamed another, which silently turned that column into the source folder.'
 '      Columns are now found by their header, so Link 3 (18.2) and Link 4 both give what they should.'
 '    * Corrections to the help: "]Cider.Version" promised name, version number and date as a'
 '      three-element vector although it returns just the version number; the syntax line and the'
 '      error message for "-watch=" both omitted "none", which has always been accepted; the syntax'
 '      line for "]Cider.AddTatinDependencies" named the command in the singular, as did the'
 '      documentation; and "]Cider.OpenProject -?" advertised "-???", which does not exist'
 '    * Corrections to the API documentation: five exported functions had no section at all'
 '      ("ReadProjectConfig", "Remove_githubUsername", "RenameInfo_url", "RunMake", "RunTests");'
 '      "ReadProjectConfig" and "WriteProjectConfig" appeared under the names they carried before'
 '      0.51.0; the argument of "GetTatinDependencies" and "GetNuGetDependencies" was given as'
 '      "development" instead of "dependencies", which returns an empty vector; "ProjectConfig" was'
 '      shown without its left argument, so the call documented there never opens an editor; and the'
 '      default of "checkPackageVersions" was the one the user command sets, not the one the API'
 '      hands out'
 '    * The `[LINK]` section of a project config file was ignored unless the file `.linkconfig` carried'
 '      Link options (since 0.46.0), and `-watch=` never reached Link as a result'
 '    * With a `.linkconfig` carrying Link options, the `[LINK]` section was applied although Cider'
 '      reported it as ignored; now it is indeed ignored'
 '    * The git status report did not report correctly the number of stashes'
 '    * `OpenProject` in batch mode carried on silently (without loading Tatin packages) when checking'
 '      the package status failed, but threw an error in interactive mode'
 '    * `]Cider.ProjectConfig <path>` ignored the path and used an open project instead'
 '    * `]Cider.ProjectConfig -edit`: cancelling caused a DOMAIN ERROR. Declining to save is now reported'
 '      as cancellation, and closing the editor without a change as "No changes"'
 '    * `ProjectConfig` wrote to the config file even in read-only mode, and crashed on a config file that'
 '      was not valid JSON5. Problems with the file are now reported as a warning'
 '    * `ProjectConfig`, `RunMake` and `RunTests` failed with a SYNTAX ERROR when called with an alias;'
 '      `RunMake` and `RunTests` did not check for an unknown alias at all'
 '    * `]Cider.AddNuGetDependencies` failed with a VALUE ERROR when called with an alias'
 '    * `]Cider.LinkConfig` crashed with a VALUE ERROR when the user cancelled the project selection'
 '    * `]Cider.OpenProject -verbose` reported a successful open as failed; the result is now empty'
 '      because the log has already been printed'
 '    * `]Cider.OpenProject [?]` reported "No aliase defined" when the user merely cancelled'
 '    * Quitting a project selection with "q" crashed `]Cider.CloseProject` and all user commands that'
 '      ask for a project (CommTools 3 returns ¯1 for "q")'
 '    * Checking a project config file (`]Cider.ProjectConfig -edit`, `]Cider.CreateProject`):'
 '      * "make" and "tests" were rejected unless the project was open, and user commands were rejected'
 '        as well'
 '      * A missing "SYSVARS" section caused a VALUE ERROR'
 '      * A problem in "dependencies_dev" could be reported as a problem in "dependencies"'
 '* 0.53.1 ⋄ 2026-08-05'
 '  * A check for Dropbox conflicts was performed no matter what the globl configuration ruled.'
 '  * Ill-formed dependency folder definitions could cause harm. Now properly reported. '
 '* 0.53.0 ⋄ 2026-07-01'
 '  * `OpenProject` and `CreateOpenParms` polished and comments clarified'
 '  * Documentation polished'
 '  * Checking project connfig file improved'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * `UC.ProjectConfig` did not print to the session when no argument was provided'
 '* 0.52.1 ⋄ 2016-05-28'
 '  * Packages updated'
 '* 0.52.0 ⋄ 2026-05-22'
 '  * All user commands carry an ]Open-statement for the correct help page'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * Fix nonsensical ]OpenProject [?] message when no aliases exist '
 '* 0.51.1 ⋄ 2026-03-04'
 '  * Fix for issue #129 including test cases'
 '* 0.51.0 ⋄ 2026-03-03'
 '  * ]ListAliases now marks folders that are not available anymore (#92)'
 '  * Aliase are now checked for starting with a letter followed by zero or more letters, digits, underscores or hyphens'
 '  * All JSON5-related stuff consolidated, see #110m for details'
 '  * Packages updated (CommTools)'
 '  * Documentation issues fixed: #109, #96, #89, #115'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * In case of a .NET error while checking Git''s status, the information available via ⎕EXCEPTION was not provided  '
 '    * On non-Windows platforms, ]ListAliases -scan=/path/2/projects failed due to an uppercase problem:'
 '      Cider looked for "Cider.config" when it should have looked for "cider.config"'
 '    * ]Listaliases -scan=/path/2/projects worked only on Windows (#128)'
 '    * Output with ⎕← has been changed to ⍞←...,⎕UCS 10 for 20.0 with array notation on for output'
 '* 0.50.1 ⋄ 2025-12-30'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * #127'
 '* 0.50.0 ⋄ 2025-12-07'
 '  * New global Cider parameter `HandleLinkStops` introduced'
 '  * `OpenProject` and `CloseProject` now both honour the global `HandleLinkStops` if set '
 '  * Cider''s test cases are now resilient against `//` in a file path, see `∆GetTestPath`'
 '  * `NuGet` package updated'
 '  * Bug fixes'
 '    * When `CreateProject` opened the project it had just created, it printed a success msg twice'
 '    * Comment in `OpenProject` corrected: read "package" when it meant "project" '
)
